# The two pilots of the Decide port (docs/adr/0091 §6, §7). KEY=VALUE, one
# per line, `#` comments on their own line. A decision whose confidence (the
# probability of its winning outcome) is under its threshold goes to a person.
#
# PERIMETER_CONFIDENCE, provenance: a measure and the owner's decision,
# 2026-11-16. On the demo intake (150 questions, gemini-decision-1) 0.8 left
# 18 and 19 paths per ticket to the person, most of them gate fixtures at
# p 0.2-0.45; 0.7 puts 5 and 4 paths in and leaves 5 and 8 uncertain.
PERIMETER_CONFIDENCE=0.7
# SCREEN_CONFIDENCE, provenance: ADR 0091's decision, the band 0.2 < p < 0.8
# left to a person; measured on the labelled set (24 texts) every answer was
# p <= 0.01 or p >= 0.97, so no text fell in the band.
SCREEN_CONFIDENCE=0.8
